WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.334 --> 00:00:07.587
Hi,  my name is Fariel,

00:00:07.587 --> 00:00:09.631
but back home,

00:00:09.631 --> 00:00:11.967
I am also called the goat lady.

00:00:12.759 --> 00:00:18.848
And today I will be sharing the story
of how that came to be about.

00:00:20.725 --> 00:00:22.686
In 2015,

00:00:22.686 --> 00:00:27.857
I visited a small,
remote village in Pakistan

00:00:27.857 --> 00:00:29.317
called Pathan Goth.

00:00:29.776 --> 00:00:32.529
The residents of Pathan Goth

00:00:32.529 --> 00:00:37.450
were living without access
to basic facilities

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:40.245
such as water and electricity.

00:00:41.037 --> 00:00:46.751
The community was bussing water
two hours from Karachi.

00:00:47.711 --> 00:00:51.131
This made their water so expensive

00:00:51.131 --> 00:00:56.553
that their livestock went
without water every other day.

00:00:58.138 --> 00:01:03.268
Bathing and laundry was a luxury.

00:01:03.643 --> 00:01:05.729
The solution was simple:

00:01:05.729 --> 00:01:07.897
a solar water pump.

00:01:08.273 --> 00:01:11.234
But that would cost $10,000.

00:01:11.693 --> 00:01:13.570
And for a community

00:01:13.570 --> 00:01:17.115
where the average household earned

00:01:17.115 --> 00:01:21.328
just about $70 a month,

00:01:21.328 --> 00:01:25.040
this was beyond their affordability.

00:01:26.541 --> 00:01:30.545
As I sat there thinking about this issue,

00:01:30.545 --> 00:01:34.674
the solution literally walked
in front of me.

00:01:35.634 --> 00:01:41.097
A herd of more than 100 goats
crossed my path.

00:01:41.806 --> 00:01:43.391
And I thought to myself,

00:01:43.391 --> 00:01:45.894
that is a lot of goats.

00:01:45.894 --> 00:01:46.895
(Laughter)

00:01:48.647 --> 00:01:53.526
I took a chance and asked
the village elder:

00:01:53.526 --> 00:01:57.989
Would they consider paying me
for their pump in goats?

00:01:58.490 --> 00:01:59.991
He agreed,

00:01:59.991 --> 00:02:04.037
and that is how Pathan Goth got its pump

00:02:04.037 --> 00:02:08.416
and I became the proud owner of 40 goats.

00:02:10.543 --> 00:02:13.880
(Applause)

00:02:14.005 --> 00:02:16.466
A few months down the line,

00:02:16.466 --> 00:02:19.386
the Muslim festival of Eid came around.

00:02:19.678 --> 00:02:23.765
During Eid, livestock is offered

00:02:23.765 --> 00:02:28.645
to honor Abraham’s willingness
to sacrifice Isaac.

00:02:29.354 --> 00:02:32.440
And much like shopping before Christmas,

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:35.026
the demand for goats goes up,

00:02:35.026 --> 00:02:37.487
and the price skyrockets.

00:02:38.363 --> 00:02:41.116
I remembered my goats

00:02:41.116 --> 00:02:45.745
and decided to put up a post on Facebook

00:02:45.745 --> 00:02:51.501
asking my friends and family
to buy their Eid goat from me that year.

00:02:52.252 --> 00:02:55.588
Within a week I sold all my goats.

00:02:55.588 --> 00:03:01.469
And even after paying for a team
to do transport and manage them,

00:03:01.469 --> 00:03:04.848
I more than recovered
the cost of the pump.

00:03:06.391 --> 00:03:12.897
This experience made me question
the idea of money

00:03:12.897 --> 00:03:16.901
and how it has changed and evolved for us.

00:03:17.777 --> 00:03:21.239
I found that in 2500 BC,

00:03:21.239 --> 00:03:23.491
Mesopotamia,

00:03:23.491 --> 00:03:28.955
Sumerians used measured
quantity of barley as money.

00:03:29.414 --> 00:03:34.586
But as the trading circle
grew beyond one village,

00:03:34.586 --> 00:03:40.049
money's key characteristics
changed and evolved.

00:03:40.425 --> 00:03:45.972
Money not only needed
to reliably store value

00:03:45.972 --> 00:03:49.225
but also be easy to convert

00:03:49.225 --> 00:03:51.853
and easy to transport.

00:03:53.021 --> 00:03:54.898
That is when we --

00:03:54.898 --> 00:03:56.357
civilization --

00:03:56.357 --> 00:03:59.569
moved towards coin and paper money.

00:04:00.361 --> 00:04:05.241
But coin and paper money get value

00:04:05.241 --> 00:04:10.038
only when they’re validated
by an external authority,

00:04:10.038 --> 00:04:15.877
such as God, crown or the central bank.

00:04:19.214 --> 00:04:22.383
Technology today enables us

00:04:22.383 --> 00:04:26.930
to bypass the need
for this central authority.

00:04:27.931 --> 00:04:32.685
Today, the value of any asset
can be transferred

00:04:32.685 --> 00:04:34.771
from one person to another

00:04:34.771 --> 00:04:36.523
using blockchain.

00:04:37.315 --> 00:04:41.152
Any asset can now be tokenized,

00:04:41.152 --> 00:04:42.570
digitized

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:43.696
and traded.

00:04:44.197 --> 00:04:50.161
So technology is not
only disrupting the need

00:04:50.161 --> 00:04:52.539
for a financial intermediary

00:04:52.539 --> 00:04:54.541
in mainstream economy

00:04:54.541 --> 00:04:57.460
but also has the potential

00:04:57.460 --> 00:05:02.131
to disrupt and democratize economic power

00:05:02.131 --> 00:05:04.342
in more rural economies.

00:05:06.177 --> 00:05:12.058
By removing the need for inefficient
and expensive intermediaries,

00:05:12.058 --> 00:05:15.937
small farmers can derive greater value

00:05:15.937 --> 00:05:18.398
from what they grow and raise.

00:05:19.774 --> 00:05:26.614
Livestock is very abundant
in these communities.

00:05:27.115 --> 00:05:31.786
Farmers literally use their goats and cows

00:05:31.786 --> 00:05:33.955
as ATM machines

00:05:33.955 --> 00:05:36.666
and as saving instruments.

00:05:37.166 --> 00:05:40.628
They will sell an animal
when they need cash,

00:05:40.628 --> 00:05:45.258
such as to buy fodder
for the rest of the herd,

00:05:45.258 --> 00:05:48.261
to buy groceries for their home

00:05:48.261 --> 00:05:52.348
or for weddings and health emergencies.

00:05:52.765 --> 00:05:56.477
But these communities have never been able

00:05:56.477 --> 00:05:59.689
to use their goats and cows

00:05:59.689 --> 00:06:03.651
for larger, more productive assets ...

00:06:03.651 --> 00:06:04.903
until now.

00:06:05.528 --> 00:06:12.452
Our farmers are able to convert
15 goats into a solar water pump.

00:06:13.453 --> 00:06:14.579
Previously,

00:06:14.579 --> 00:06:18.416
these communities would rely on

00:06:18.416 --> 00:06:21.044
or wait for an NGO,

00:06:21.044 --> 00:06:22.295
a charity

00:06:22.295 --> 00:06:26.090
or the government to take notice

00:06:26.090 --> 00:06:28.384
and give them what they needed.

00:06:28.718 --> 00:06:34.557
Now they are using their own resources

00:06:34.557 --> 00:06:39.354
to fulfill their own needs
when they need it.

00:06:39.771 --> 00:06:42.065
This is self-reliance.

00:06:42.774 --> 00:06:49.238
(Applause and cheers)

00:06:50.573 --> 00:06:55.328
So how have we enabled the use of goats

00:06:55.328 --> 00:06:57.997
as a reliable form of currency?

00:06:58.665 --> 00:07:04.128
Right now, we we work with farmers
through physical barter.

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:08.675
At the time of the solar installation,

00:07:08.675 --> 00:07:12.011
we take possession of the goats.

00:07:12.512 --> 00:07:17.392
We then sell these goats
as meat to grocery chains

00:07:17.392 --> 00:07:20.186
and through our own retail brand.

00:07:21.938 --> 00:07:27.360
Every goat that we receive
is then recorded,

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:29.862
as its unique ID --

00:07:29.862 --> 00:07:35.368
its key characteristics such as its sex,

00:07:35.368 --> 00:07:36.452
its age,

00:07:36.452 --> 00:07:37.453
its weight

00:07:37.453 --> 00:07:41.374
and even its number of teeth
are taken into account.

00:07:41.499 --> 00:07:43.543
And then using these,

00:07:43.543 --> 00:07:48.798
we assign each goat
a dollar or a rupee value,

00:07:48.798 --> 00:07:51.676
essentially tokenizing a goat.

00:07:53.594 --> 00:07:59.475
We have already worked
with 45 communities,

00:07:59.475 --> 00:08:03.146
enabling more than 6,000 farmers

00:08:03.146 --> 00:08:08.026
to convert their goats
into water and electricity.

00:08:08.317 --> 00:08:14.991
(Applause)

00:08:15.324 --> 00:08:19.120
We are now planning to add smartphones,

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:20.246
tractors

00:08:20.246 --> 00:08:22.373
and other equipment.

00:08:23.541 --> 00:08:30.089
My hope is that we can create
a more inclusive economic system

00:08:30.089 --> 00:08:31.674
where any person

00:08:31.674 --> 00:08:38.473
or any community can use
what they grow and raise as money.

00:08:39.307 --> 00:08:42.268
Where a farmer, a small farmer

00:08:42.518 --> 00:08:44.687
can use, wherever he is,

00:08:44.687 --> 00:08:47.482
whether it’s Pakistan, Nepal, Somalia,

00:08:47.482 --> 00:08:54.072
can use a digitized goat
to pay for her kid’s school fees,

00:08:54.072 --> 00:08:55.156
a tractor

00:08:55.156 --> 00:08:56.491
or a smartphone.

00:08:56.866 --> 00:09:00.078
This future isn't quite here yet,

00:09:00.078 --> 00:09:04.707
but I hope using goats
as money gets us closer.

00:09:04.707 --> 00:09:05.708
Thank you.

00:09:05.708 --> 00:09:12.507
(Applause and cheers)

